# khatinews.com — Cursor project rules

You are working on **khatinews.com**, a Bangladesh-focused news intelligence product: multi-source headline clusters, perspective/bias signals, rumor flags, blindspot detection, and **AI claim verification**. Installable **PWA**; UI is English + Bangla where the app already uses both.

**Detailed rules** live in `.cursor/rules/` (`khatinews.mdc` always applies; `backend.mdc` / `frontend.mdc` / `supabase.mdc` / **`chrome-extension.mdc`** when editing those trees). Maintainer guide: `docs/CURSOR_RULES.md`.

## Architecture

- `backend/` — Python 3.11+, FastAPI, async SQLAlchemy, PostgreSQL (+ **pgvector** / FTS for verified claims), optional **Redis** + **Celery** (ingest + verification queues), RSS ingestion (`app/services/rss_ingestion.py`: **`feed_urls_for_source`** pulls primary + seed **`additional_feed_urls`**; `rss_parser.fetch_feed_items` follows redirects with a browser User-Agent; clusters match on title overlap or **`story_match.py`** across Bangla and English, then prefer a Bangla cluster title; each distinct article headline is stored on **`article_titles`** for later features), Groq/Gemini via `app/services/ai_client.py`; one outlet per row in `app/data/bd_sources_seed.py` (names mirrored by `frontend/src/lib/seed-source-names.ts`); `POST /api/v1/ingest` + `npm run ingest:backend`
- `frontend/` — Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, optional Supabase auth (`src/lib/supabase.ts`, `database.types.ts`, `/sign-in`, `/sign-up`)
- `supabase/` — migrations for profiles, Pro subscriptions, PayEurasia payment records, user dossiers/alerts (news + verified claims stay in backend Postgres)
- Root scripts: `npm run dev:frontend`, `dev:backend`, `ingest:backend`, **`worker:backend`**, **`worker:beat`**, **`worker:verification`**, **`stack:up`** / **`stack:down`** (`docker-compose.yml`: Postgres pgvector, Redis, API, Celery worker, **beat** for scheduled RSS)
- **Production releases**: `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` (deploy order, migrations, rollback, checklist)
- **Claim verification**: `POST /api/v1/verify` (guardrailed submit), `/api/v1/verifications/*` (jobs, SSE/WS, list/search/detail); UI `/verify`, `/verify/[slug]`, `/verify/database` via `src/lib/verifications.ts`
- **Public sources**: `GET /api/v1/sources` (optional `custom_only`) + `GET /api/v1/articles?source_id=` — admin-added RSS and per-source article reads (no admin key); optional helper `fetchCustomSourcesFeed` in `api.ts`
- **Admin ops (internal)**: backend `GET /api/v1/admin/overview` (includes **`ingest_schedule`**) + **`GET/PATCH /api/v1/admin/ingest-schedule`** (`app_settings`, migration `003_app_settings.sql`; Celery beat tick when `REDIS_URL` + `INGEST_SCHEDULER_ENABLED`) + RSS source add/remove/update (`admin.py` → `admin_stats` / `admin_sources` / **`ingest_schedule`**; **`PATCH /admin/sources/{id}`**, **`POST .../import`** for feed files; **`ingest_mode`** `rss` \| `file`, migration `005_sources_ingest_mode.sql`, **`006_sources_ownership.sql`**; DELETE purges articles/orphan clusters then soft-disables seed or deletes custom; `sources.disabled`, migration `002_sources_disabled.sql`); scheduled/per-source RSS pull skips **`file`** sources (`source_ingest_mode.py`); frontend **`admin.khatinews.com`** in production (`admin-host.ts`, local `/admin`) gated by legacy cookie or **Supabase admin**; tabbed **`AdminDashboardPanel`** (overview, sources/ingest, system, **Users**, issues) + `GET /api/admin/overview` → `{ overview, apiHealthy }`; legacy **`shorup_admin`** cookie still required for sources/ingest/**ingest-schedule**/users proxies (overview allows Supabase admin — see `frontend.mdc`); optional **`chrome-extension/prothomalo-feed-collector`** exports JSON for admin file upload (bundled BD catalog in **`lib/bd-sources.js`**, enabled unless unchecked)
- **PWA deploy resilience**: `chunk-load-error.ts` — one-shot reload on chunk failures (`error.tsx` / `global-error.tsx`; dev SW unregister in `layout.tsx`); see `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`
- **Monitoring (optional)**: Sentry on backend (`app/core/sentry_init.py`) and frontend (`@sentry/nextjs`, `instrumentation.ts`); ingest cron pings via `app/services/ops_alerts.py` (Healthchecks.io + Telegram when env is set)

## Conventions

### Backend
- Thin routes in `app/api/`; logic in `app/services/`; schemas in `app/schemas/`; models in `app/models/`
- Async for I/O; config in `app/core/config.py`; API prefix `/api/v1`; optional `INGEST_API_KEY` / `ADMIN_API_KEY`; Redis-backed rate limits when `REDIS_URL` is set; never commit secrets

### Frontend
- Pages under `frontend/src/app/`; components in `src/components/`; route errors in `app/error.tsx`, `app/global-error.tsx`, and `app/not-found.tsx`; segment `loading.tsx` on story/verify detail
- Fetch via `api.ts` + `api-resilience.ts`, `stories.ts` (API + `demo-data.ts` fallback, `fromApi` + `ApiDegradedBanner`; **`applySourceDerivedSummaries`** → RSS **`summaryBullets`** + perspective digests; **`mixed-script-text`** + **`client-story-hydrate`** for **`titleBn`** / localStorage cache); articles may include RSS `image_url`; cluster detail `source_name` / `bias_score` / `owner_name` (and parent) for blindspot, partiality, and ownership; story detail **`StoryDetailMetaBar`**, the sharper of **`SharedOwnershipReveal`** / **`UnnamedSourceReveal`** (**`pickSharpestRevealKind`**), **`StoryCoverageBlock`**, **`AntiClickbaitSummaryPanel`**, **`StoryFollowButton`**, **`StoryShareBar`**, **`StoryTabs`**; public OG is the free square card from **`story-share-card.ts`** + **`opengraph-image.tsx`**; each **`StoryShareBar`** network sends **`GET /api/story/[slug]/share-card`** when the browser can share a file, otherwise that network’s link; copy-link stays a URL; verification via `verifications.ts`
- Pro tier: `subscription-features.ts` (matrix, `PRO_ONLY_FEATURE_IDS`: **`follow_story`**, **`track_article_clicks`**, **`story_shared_ownership_alerts`**, **`story_unnamed_source`**, **`story_taken_down_vault`**, **`first_headline`**, **`custom_topic_radar_alerts`**); `subscription-plans.ts` (৳15/24h day pass, ৳49/mo, ৳399/yr); `subscription-access.ts` + **`GET /api/me/pro`** for client gates, `NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_PRO`; **`/pro`** + **`PaywallModal`** (`featureId`); **`followed-stories.ts`** / **`followed-topics.ts`** / **`follow-people.ts`** (localStorage until server sync); **`/profile`** + **`reading-history.ts`** (device-local bias dashboard)
- Home: Bangla hero + **`HeaderBanglaDate`**; **`HomeTopicFilter`** + **`HomeStoryGridClient`** (**`StoryFeedCard`** **`variant="home"`**) → **`/api/feed/top`** + **`/api/me/pro`**; **`SiteHeader`** EN tagline (not Bangla date); **`.story-title-bn`** in **`globals.css`**
- Server components for feeds; client components for interactive UI — wrap fragile client trees in `ClientErrorBoundary`
- Reads degrade to demo when the API is down; writes (verify submit, admin) must surface real failures

## Product vocabulary

- **Cluster / headline clash** — Same story, different framings. Bangla and English papers stay in one cluster
- **Story language** — The story title readers see is Bangla when any Bangla headline exists (`deriveTitleBn`). Each outlet’s headline stays in the language it was published in. English-only stories keep the English title. Do not add a Bangla/English feed switch, and do not translate every article title
- **Perspective** — `neutral` \| `establishment` \| `opposition` \| `international`. Political stories use a government spectrum (for government → against government → neutral → international). Other topics use a reporting spectrum (Clickbait → Mixed → Factual → Rumor) via `reporting-spectrum.ts` on `CoverageBar` and **`StoryArticleFeed`**
- **Bias meter** — Scored lean for a source or cluster
- **Rumor badge** — Unverified or speculative coverage
- **Blindspot** — Establishment or opposition press missing while the other side dominates (`blindspot.ts`; `/blindspot` feed)
- **Partiality** — Any perspective bucket still empty in a multi-source cluster (`partiality.ts`; banners/teasers on story detail and feed cards)
- **Shared ownership** — Two or more outlets in one cluster share an owner or parent. The story page shows this only when it is the sharper reveal (`pickSharpestRevealKind`; ownership wins a tie). Everyone sees the count (`4 outlets, 2 owners`); Pro sees the names (`SharedOwnershipReveal`, `story_shared_ownership_alerts`)
- **Unnamed source** — Headline or excerpt contains “সূত্র”, “নাম প্রকাশে অনিচ্ছুক”, “সংশ্লিষ্ট”, or “sources say”. Shown on the story page only when it is the sharper reveal. Everyone sees the count (`4 of 6 outlets attribute this to someone they don't name.`); Pro sees which papers hid the name and which outlet printed one (`UnnamedSourceReveal`, `story_unnamed_source`)
- **Taken-down vault** — A page that was deleted or now 404s stays on the card (`removedAt`). Everyone sees `Removed from their site at 6:40pm.`; Pro sees the original headline and text (`This is what it said at 1:12pm.`). Preview story `desk-pulled-the-page` (`TakenDownVault`, `story_taken_down_vault`)
- **Line under the headline** — Sentence after the outrage that starts with “তবে”, “অন্যদিকে”, or “নাম প্রকাশে অনিচ্ছুক একটি সূত্র” (`WalkbackPin`). Everyone sees it above the headline. Pro share cards use it as the line (`story_walkback_line`)
- **Verified claim** — Completed fact-check with verdict + analysis (`/verify/[slug]`, backend `verified_claims`)
- **Anti-clickbait summary** — Up to three neutral bullets from RSS excerpts/headlines (`buildAntiClickbaitBullets`); not AI-generated
- **First headline** — First wording and share card stay from the moment a story appears. A later edit with no correction still shows both lines and the clock. Free sees those lines; Pro sees the frozen social preview (`first_headline` on `/pro`)
- **khatinews Pro** — Full news for everyone; Pro unlocks **`PRO_ONLY_FEATURE_IDS`** (`follow_story`, `track_article_clicks`, `story_shared_ownership_alerts`, `story_unnamed_source`, `story_taken_down_vault`, `first_headline`, `custom_topic_radar_alerts`). Plans: ৳15/24h day pass, ৳49/mo, ৳399/yr — matrix on `/pro`

## Quality bar

- Match existing layout and naming; minimal diffs; no drive-by refactors
- Type hints on Python public functions; strict TypeScript on frontend
